<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>

    <PackageId>FlappyBird</PackageId>
    <Version>2.0.0</Version>
    <Authors>TranDat1114</Authors>
    <Description>A Flappy Bird game for console — with themes, two-player split screen, custom game configuration, and a persistent high score board.</Description>
    <Copyright>Copyright © 2025 TranDat1114</Copyright>
    <PackageTags>game;console;flappybird;retro;dotnet-tool</PackageTags>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/TranDat1114/FlappyBird</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/TranDat1114/FlappyBird</PackageProjectUrl>

    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
v2.0.0 (2026-06-30):
- Custom Game mode: configure starting level (1-10) or manual Speed/Gap; difficulty fixed in Manual mode
- High Scores: persistent leaderboard of last 1000 sessions; paginated (10/page), filterable by mode
- Settings persistence: all settings saved to %AppData%\FlappyBird\settings.json between sessions
- Theme system: 4 built-in themes (Classic, Matrix, Neon, Retro) applied to menus and game borders
- Dynamic border styles: game borders now follow the selected theme (Rounded, Single, ASCII, Double)
- TwoPlayer pipe spacing fixed: visual density now matches SinglePlayer
- Font management, audio calibration menu
- English / Vietnamese localization
- Responsive layout with resize detection

v1.1.0:
- Two Player local co-op (split screen, P1: W / P2: Up Arrow)
- Audio: Harry Potter background music, sound effects (NAudio on Windows)
- Dual AI Comparison mode (conservative vs aggressive, 10-round tournament)
- God Mode rule-based AI; Q-Learning agent with JSONL training logger

v1.0.0:
- Initial release: Single Player, 60 FPS, realistic physics, progressive difficulty
    </PackageReleaseNotes>

    <!-- Global Tool Configuration -->
    <PackAsTool>true</PackAsTool>
    <ToolCommandName>flappybird</ToolCommandName>

    <!-- Icon and README -->
    <PackageIcon>bird.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="bird.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NAudio" Version="2.2.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Copy audio files to output so AudioManager can play them at runtime -->
    <Content Include="Resources\Audio\*.mp3" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest">
      <Link>Resources\Audio\%(Filename)%(Extension)</Link>
    </Content>

    <!-- Copy font files to output so FontManager.Scan() can find them at runtime -->
    <Content Include="Resources\Fonts\**\*.ttf" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest">
      <Link>Resources\Fonts\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)</Link>
    </Content>
    <Content Include="Resources\Fonts\**\*.otf" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest">
      <Link>Resources\Fonts\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)</Link>
    </Content>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>